  "factor_name": "Breadth-conditioned drawdown recovery",
  "version": "1.0",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "lag1((close / rolling_min(close,60) - 1) / rolling_std(log_return,30)) with sign gated by lag1(rolling_mean(cross_sectional_positive_return_breadth,10)) > 0.50",
    "description": "Ranks assets by recovery from their 60-session low, risk-adjusted by 30-session volatility. When lagged market breadth is weak, reverses the signal to avoid chasing rebounds in deteriorating regimes. All inputs are lagged one completed session before use."
